# The chords alone, written for gohar from the analysis of En Harmonie:
# three II-V-I a tone apart, to D, to C, to B♭, and back to D.
{start_of_grid label="A" shape="4x4"}
| Em7 | A7 | Dmaj7 | Dmaj7 |
| Dm7 | G7 | Cmaj7 | Cmaj7 |
| Cm7 | F7 | Bbmaj7 | Gm7 |
| Em7 | A7 | Dmaj7 | Dmaj7 |.
{end_of_grid}
